<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Caucasus</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of Kars</h1><p class="st-meta">963 CE – 1065 CE · capital Kars</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">A small Armenian kingdom centred on the fortress city of Kars, ruled by a junior Bagratid line until it was handed to Byzantium.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 963 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashot-iii-of-armenia">Ashot III of Bagratid Armenia</a> gave the district of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vanand">Vanand</a>, with the fortress of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a>, to his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mushegh-of-kars">Mushegh</a>, who took the title king. The kingdom remained linked to the senior line at Ani while governing its own affairs.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a> was a strong fortress town on the route from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anatolia">Anatolia</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a>, and its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/church-of-the-holy-apostles-kars">Cathedral of the Holy Apostles</a>, built by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abas-i-of-armenia">Abas</a> in the 930s-40s when Kars was still the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bagratuni-dynasty">Bagratid</a> capital, dominated the city. The kings ruled local nobles and peasants and acted as allies and rivals of the kings at Ani.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>After <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a> annexed Ani in 1045 and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seljuk-empire">Seljuks</a> sacked it in 1064, King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gagik-abas-of-kars">Gagik-Abas</a> surrendered <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kars">Kars</a> to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantine-empire">Byzantine Empire</a> in 1065 for lands in <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-cappadocia">Cappadocia</a>. The Seljuks took the city soon after.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-kars.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Kars" width="320" height="249"><figcaption>Image: Don-kun · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Caucasus_1060_map_alt_de.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>963 CE – 1065 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kars</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Mushegh, Abas, Gagik-Abas</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Armenian Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Armenian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Turkey</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Kingdom of Vanand, Kars Kingdom</dd></dl></aside></div>
